Memory rules:
- separate current situation facts from longer-term tendencies
- do not turn one-off facts into durable traits too quickly
- only surface old memory when family/demension overlap is strong
- if relevance is weak, skip the memory line
- suppress overused generic pattern lines aggressively
- do not let style memory substitute for missing same-family decision evidence